<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  launchd USER AGENT for the ctxroute HTTP injection gate. EAGER MODEL —
  the DELIBERATE ALTERNATIVE to `com.ctxroute.http.plist` (socket-activated,
  the DEFAULT). Read this whole header before choosing this file: it trades
  one real, measured protection for another, it does not add one for free.
  ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  🔴 WHY THIS FILE EXISTS (2026-09-17). `com.ctxroute.http.plist`'s Sockets
     dictionary was checked key by key against launchd.plist(5): SockType,
     SockPassive, SockNodeName, SockServiceName, SockFamily, SockProtocol,
     SockPathName, SecureSocketWithKey, SockPathOwner, SockPathGroup,
     SockPathMode, Bonjour, MulticastGroup — NONE governs the listen queue
     size. launchd itself calls listen() on that socket before handing it to
     the shim, with an internal default neither documented nor configurable.
     That is a REAL, sourced ceiling this project cannot see or raise while
     socket-activated on macOS.

  ⚠️ THE TRADE, STATED PLAINLY, NOT HIDDEN BEHIND THE FIX IT BUYS:
     ✅ GAINED: `http-server.js`'s own `LISTEN_BACKLOG = 65535` applies here,
        identically to Windows — full control over the accept queue.
     🔴 LOST: the socket-activated file's whole reason to exist. THIS file
        binds and listens ONLY while the node process itself is alive, so
        every death (`EXIT_STALE_CODE = 90`, fired on the daemon's OWN code
        changing on disk — routine mid-refactor, several times a minute) has
        NOTHING listening between exit and respawn. A tool call landing in
        that window gets a refused connection with NO carryover possible —
        `com.ctxroute.http.plist`'s header documents this as the exact
        defect socket activation was built to remove. It is NOT fixed here.
     ⇒ Choose this file only where the accept-queue ceiling is the more
        likely failure than a stale-code respawn window (e.g. a machine that
        never edits this repository, so `EXIT_STALE_CODE` essentially never
        fires) — never as a blanket "better" default.

  🛑 NOT YET RUN ON A REAL MAC (2026-09-17) — verify via
     `.github/workflows/service-units.yml` (a rented macOS runner) before
     treating this as proven; the existing socket-activated file already has
     that job, this one does not yet. Add a job for THIS file before
     deploying it anywhere real. See `service/README.md`.
  ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>

    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.ctxroute.http.eager</string>

    <!--
      ⚠️ NO SHIM HERE — read why in the header above before adding one back.
         `launch_activate_socket` only matters for a socket launchd itself
         pre-binds; this file never declares a Sockets dictionary, so node
         binds its OWN port directly, exactly like the Windows eager model
         (`http-server.js`'s `listenOn` / `server.listen(port, host,
         LISTEN_BACKLOG)`). ABSOLUTE PATHS, substituted by the installer —
         never edit the placeholder below by hand.
    -->
    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/usr/local/bin/node</string>
        <string>/Users/CHANGE_ME/ctxroute/src/hooks/http-daemon.js</string>
    </array>

    <!--
      ⚠️ RunAtLoad + KeepAlive ARE HERE ON PURPOSE — the exact pair the
         socket-activated file documents removing, and removes for a real
         reason (see its own header). Re-reading that header before touching
         this pair is mandatory, not optional prose.
      🛑 SuccessfulExit = false: `EXIT_STALE_CODE` (90) is NOT a clean exit in
         this model — with no socket held elsewhere, a respawn is the ONLY
         way back, so unlike the socket-activated file, KeepAlive MUST select
         on it. A zero-status exit (an operator's deliberate stop) must NOT
         respawn, which is exactly what `SuccessfulExit = false` expresses:
         "restart only when the job exits ON ITS OWN with a NON-zero status"
         (TN2083's own phrasing).
    -->
    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <true/>
    <key>KeepAlive</key>
    <dict>
        <key>SuccessfulExit</key>
        <false/>
    </dict>

    <!--
      ⚠️ THE PORT IS NOT WRITTEN HERE — this model reads it from the SAME
         single resolution point every other lane does (`paths.httpEndpoint()`
         in the daemon's own config), never a second copy in a plist. Only the
         socket-activated file needs `SockServiceName`, because only it is the
         one BINDING the port on launchd's behalf.
    -->

    <!--
      LOG BOUNDING — identical reasoning to the socket-activated file.
      StandardOutPath / StandardErrorPath stay ABSENT: launchd redirects to
      ASL (TN2083), macOS caps and rotates it, we do not reimplement that.
      🛑 Never write a double hyphen inside a plist XML comment — it is
         malformed XML by the DTD, measured 2026-08-23 on the sibling file.
    -->

</dict>
</plist>
